Fillets: an end where the face at the end goes on tangentially from a
face of the spine's edge is an OnSame end (mitcad#343).

The case: a pin of radius 4.5 standing out of a wall, rounded at its foot
with 1 (a concave rounding), whose foot's arc ends where the wall ends in
a slot: the slot's sides are planes tangent to the pin along the lines
through the arc's end vertices, so at each end the wall's edge with the
slot's side runs into the vertex tangent to the arc (the wall a cusp
there), and the slot's side goes on tangentially from the pin across
their common edge. The bodies stored in the file cut the rounding by the
slot's side, which grows up to it along that edge prolonged (to where the
rounding's contact on the pin crosses it): the torus runs on to both ends.

ChFi3d_EdgeState decides the end's state from the faces' sides at the two
other edges of the vertex, sampled inside each edge; at an edge between
tangent faces those sides follow no rule, and the end was OnDiff here. The
walk past the wall's edge then rolled on that edge into the vertex (a
blend ending in a point there, 0770) or ended on the pin's seam far round,
and the corner walked round the vertex: the result was off the file's by
0.14 or invalid. Where exactly one of the two edges lies between faces
tangent to each other and leaves the vertex behind the spine's edge (on
the side away from the interior of the face it shares with the spine's
edge, whose corner there is reflex: the blend's contact on that face does
not reach it, ChFi3d_TangentEdgeBehindSpine), the end is now OnSame: the
face at the end cuts the blend and grows up to it along the tangent edge
prolonged (PerformOneCorner's OnSame end, whose tangent case seeks the
contact's crossing with that edge). Where such an edge leaves into that
face (an earlier rounding of one of its other edges coming in at the
vertex), the contact runs onto the face at the end before the vertex and
the state is decided as before. On the stored body before the rounding:
the file's change of volume within 2.4e-4 mm3 and every new face on the
file's within 1e-5.

Upstream: new.
